[
{ type: install
  message: <<EOM
The virtio_gpu_qemu driver has been installed, but it does nothing until it is
preloaded.  Add the following to /boot/loader.conf and reboot:

	virtio_gpu_qemu_load="YES"

Optionally override the display resolution advertised by the host, and set the
framebuffer flush rate in frames per second:

	hw.virtio_gpu_qemu.width="1536"
	hw.virtio_gpu_qemu.height="864"
	hw.virtio_gpu_qemu.refresh_rate="30"

The module MUST be preloaded by loader(8).  Loading it later from kld_list in
rc.conf is not enough: by then the in-kernel VirtIO GPU driver has already
claimed the device and taken the console.

To run an X server on this display you also need the scfb video driver, which
is provided by one of two mutually exclusive ports.  Install whichever matches
your X server:

	x11-drivers/xf86-video-scfb		for Xorg
	x11-drivers/xlibre-xf86-video-scfb	for Xlibre

The X configuration selecting it has been installed as:

	%%PREFIX%%/share/X11/xorg.conf.d/20-virtio-gpu-qemu.conf

It is only read when an X server runs.  To override it, place a file of the
same name in %%PREFIX%%/etc/X11/xorg.conf.d, which is searched first; to
disable it, remove it.

Note that the module cannot be unloaded once it owns the system console;
kldunload(8) will fail with EBUSY.  Changing the resolution therefore requires
editing loader.conf and rebooting.

See virtio_gpu_qemu(4) for details.
EOM
}
]
